# rakuten-scraper — copy to .env and fill in what you need.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# NOTHING HERE IS REQUIRED to scrape this site. Measured 2026-09-21 from a
# datacentre address with no key, no proxy and no account: a keyword search
# returned 45 products a page and a three-page run returned 135 rows with
# 100% price coverage. Every variable below buys volume, a Japanese exit or a
# consistent device identity — not access.
#
# A credential belongs in this file and NEVER on a command line: anything
# that can run `ps` can read an argv, and shell history keeps it.
#
# Check what was picked up, without printing any of it:
#
#   python3 env_config.py
#
# Precedence, highest first:
#   an explicit flag  ->  an exported environment variable  ->  .env  ->  the
#   default
#
# So a `.env` never overrides something you typed, and an already-exported
# variable (a CI secret, direnv, your shell profile) is never clobbered by a
# file someone forgot to delete.

# --- 2Captcha, one key for four separately-billed products ---------------
# Solving, the Scraping Browser API, proxies and fingerprints all sit behind
# this one key. https://2captcha.com/enterpage
#
# On THIS site there is nothing for the solver to do, and that is measured
# rather than assumed: no captcha of any kind is configured anywhere on
# rakuten.co.jp — zero reCAPTCHA, hCaptcha, Turnstile, DataDome, PerimeterX,
# Incapsula, Kasada or AWS WAF markers across 13 captures, served and refused
# alike — and Akamai's refusal here is a 43-byte page with no widget on it.
# The key is still worth having for the proxy and Scraping Browser products,
# and detection stays wired in case that changes between deploys.
TWOCAPTCHA_KEY=your_2captcha_api_key_here

# --- The Scraping Browser API (a managed browser over CDP) ---------------
# The endpoint SHAPE, not a working endpoint. A profile's credentials do
# expire (how long they last varies; do not plan around a fixed figure), and
# a stale endpoint produces an auth error (HTTP 401) a long way from its
# cause. Get fresh ones from the dashboard.
#
#   country-xx  picks the exit country. `country-jp` for a Japanese exit.
#   pid-...     is a profile with persistent cookies. ONE live connection
#               each, so reuse pids rather than minting one per run, and do
#               not raise --concurrency above 1 with this set.
#
# Do NOT add --fingerprint or a custom user agent on top of this: the remote
# browser already has an identity, and stacking a second one manufactures the
# one thing Akamai refuses here — a client that contradicts itself. The
# engines ignore the flag with --cdp-endpoint and say so.
#
# Used on its own, --fingerprint is measured to WORK here (2026-09-21: served
# 90 rows over two pages, with the page reporting the fingerprint's own user
# agent, timezone, platform and languages). It is a COMPLETE identity that is
# fine; half of one is not.
RAKUTEN_CDP_ENDPOINT=ws://{login}-zone-scraping_browser-country-jp-pid-{profileId}:{password}@cb.2captcha.com:9222

# --- A proxy exit --------------------------------------------------------
# Not needed for the routes this scraper reads — one datacentre address was
# served the full catalogue by both plain curl and headless Chromium. Worth
# having for VOLUME: Rakuten answers a client going too fast with HTTP 503
# and its own "access is concentrated" page, and spreading a run across exits
# is how you avoid meeting it.
#
# The value below is the documented SHAPE. Take the real one from the
# dashboard — the `{...}` parts are what you fill in, and env_config treats
# any value still containing braces as unset, so a copied example is never
# sent to the API as if it were a credential.
#
# The host is a GATEWAY (ap, na or eu), not a country: a Japanese exit is
# chosen by the `-region-jp` segment the dashboard puts in the login, not by
# the hostname. Checked 2026-10-29 with a credential-free CONNECT to port
# 2334: ap/na/eu answer `407 Proxy Authentication Required` (a real gateway);
# `jp.proxy.2captcha.com` resolves to the same Cloudflare addresses as the
# 2captcha website and the connection times out.
#
# Put the real value ON THIS LINE. A second RAKUTEN_PROXY line further down
# also works (the last one is used, and a warning names the repeat), but a
# file holding both is harder to read than one.
RAKUTEN_PROXY=http://{user}-zone-custom-region-jp:{password}@ap.proxy.2captcha.com:2334

# --- A default URL ------------------------------------------------------
# Saves typing `--url` on every run. An explicit --url always wins.
RAKUTEN_URL=https://search.rakuten.co.jp/search/mall/%E3%82%B3%E3%83%BC%E3%83%92%E3%83%BC/
